ers:** Limits on deviation from the standard basket, pricing and valuation methods, and treatment of cash and tax implications.\n\n**Review roles:** Board (or its delegate) oversight of the policies, with compliance and portfolio-management responsibilities assigned.\n\n**Compliance records:** Documentation of each custom basket, its rationale, approvals, and adherence to the policies, retained under the fund's recordkeeping obligations.\n\n**Custom basket vs. non-standard order:** A custom basket differs in composition from the fund's standard creation/redemption basket. A non-standard order is generally a deviation in terms (timing, cash component, or fees) within an otherwise standard basket. Confirm classification with counsel, since the rule's terms should be checked against the current text.","ttft_ms":5734,"type":"result","duration_ms":7423,"uuid":"73abefb9-1ace-4767-8043-37f7f3e11ec9","ttft_stream_ms":387,"time_to_request_ms":54,"first_content_frame_ms":388,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
